{"id":"69a39ee9-d979-4604-9053-19c238200782","createdAt":"2026-10-26T13:32:41.699Z","batchId":"profile_gpt-6-luna_medium","approach":"html","modelId":"gpt-6-luna","settings":{"effort":"medium"},"presetId":"profile","prompt":"A user profile card with avatar, name, role, short bio, a few stats and a follow button.","system":"Return only the body content of an HTML page: no doctype, <html>, <head> or <body> tags, no markdown, no code fences, no prose. The page shell below is already loaded, so build with its classes and chart helper. Inline <script> is allowed for interactivity (tabs, toggles, filters); no external requests. Add a small <style> block only for what the classes cannot express, or when the request asks for a different look, colours, fonts or layout: then follow the request.\nPAGE SHELL (already loaded; do not restate it):\n- A stylesheet with these classes. Use them instead of writing CSS:\n  layout: page (centered column), stack, row, between, center, gap-sm, gap-lg, grid + cols-2|cols-3|cols-4 (responsive)\n  surfaces: card, card-title, card-desc, alert, alert-destructive, hr\n  text: h1-h4 (styled), lead, muted, small, up, down (trend colours)\n  controls: btn, btn-secondary|btn-outline|btn-ghost|btn-destructive, btn-sm|btn-lg, btn-block; label wraps input/select/textarea; label.check wraps a checkbox or radio\n  data: table (styled; td.num for numbers), badge, badge-secondary|badge-outline|badge-destructive, stat-label, stat-value, progress (inner div with style=\"width:NN%\"), avatar\n- Charts: <div data-chart='{\"type\":\"bar|line|area|pie\",\"title\":\"…\",\"data\":[{\"label\":\"W1\",\"value\":120}]}'></div> renders an SVG chart (single series, pie gets a legend). Do not draw charts yourself.\n- Light and dark mode are handled by the stylesheet.\n\nDESIGN BRIEF (applies to every UI you produce):\n- Build a complete, realistic screen, not a skeleton: a clear title and intro, grouped sections, and enough detail that it could ship.\n- Cover exactly what the request names, with no extra pages or marketing sections.\n- Use the supplied DATA in full: every field is there to be shown. Derive useful extras from it (shares, totals, deltas, rankings) instead of inventing unrelated numbers.\n- Where it fits, add status badges, trend/change figures, secondary actions, helper text, and sensible empty or edge-case copy.\n- Establish hierarchy with headings, size and weight; group related items; keep spacing and alignment consistent.\n- Make charts readable: a title, labelled axes or values, and a legend for pie charts.\n- Never use lorem ipsum or placeholder names like \"Item 1\".","systemHash":"0c16911c9564c3db3ada7a622931ee6ffc820ebf9a373996782a9f1f0fc3c98c","systemOverridden":false,"strictOutput":false,"rawOutput":"<main class=\"page stack gap-lg\">\n  <header class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n    <h1 class=\"h1\">Community profile</h1>\n    <p class=\"lead\">Get to know Maya and follow her updates.</p>\n  </header>\n\n  <section class=\"card stack gap-lg\" aria-labelledby=\"profile-name\">\n    <div class=\"row between gap-lg\">\n      <div class=\"row gap-lg\">\n        <div class=\"avatar\" aria-label=\"Maya Chen\">MC</div>\n        <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n          <div class=\"row gap-sm\">\n            <h2 class=\"h2\" id=\"profile-name\">Maya Chen</h2>\n            <span class=\"badge badge-secondary\">Verified</span>\n          </div>\n          <p class=\"card-desc\">Product Designer</p>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <button class=\"btn btn-primary\" id=\"follow-button\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\">Follow</button>\n    </div>\n\n    <p>Maya designs thoughtful digital experiences and shares notes on accessibility, creative process, and the little details that make products feel human.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"grid cols-3 gap-lg\" aria-label=\"Profile stats\">\n      <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n        <span class=\"stat-value\">86</span>\n        <span class=\"stat-label\">Posts</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n        <span class=\"stat-value\" id=\"follower-count\" data-count=\"2418\">2,418</span>\n        <span class=\"stat-label\">Followers</span>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n        <span class=\"stat-value\">312</span>\n        <span class=\"stat-label\">Following</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </section>\n</main>\n\n<script>\n  const followButton = document.getElementById(\"follow-button\");\n  const followerCount = document.getElementById(\"follower-count\");\n\n  followButton.addEventListener(\"click\", () => {\n    const following = followButton.getAttribute(\"aria-pressed\") === \"true\";\n    const count = Number(followerCount.dataset.count) + (following ? -1 : 1);\n\n    followerCount.dataset.count = count;\n    followerCount.textContent = count.toLocaleString();\n    followButton.setAttribute(\"aria-pressed\", String(!following));\n    followButton.textContent = following ? \"Follow\" : \"Following\";\n    followButton.classList.toggle(\"btn-primary\", following);\n    followButton.classList.toggle(\"btn-secondary\", !following);\n  });\n</script>","deltas":[[4586,"<"],[4589,"main"],[4597," class"],[4606,"=\""],[4606,"page"],[4608," stack"],[4612," gap"],[4616,"-lg"],[4617,"\">\n"],[4622," "],[4629," <"],[4634,"header"],[4636," class"],[4640,"=\""],[4643,"stack"],[4647," gap"],[4649,"-sm"],[4651,"\">\n"],[4689,"   "],[4689," <"],[4689,"h"],[4689,"1"],[4689," class"],[4689,"=\""],[4689,"h"],[4689,"1"],[4712,"\">"],[4712,"Community"],[4712," profile"],[4712,"</"],[4712,"h"],[4712,"1"],[4712,">\n"],[4712,"   "],[4728," <"],[4728,"p"],[4728," class"],[4728,"=\""],[4728,"lead"],[4728,"\">"],[4728,"Get"],[4728," to"],[4728," know"],[4728," Maya"],[4728," and"],[4728," follow"],[4728," her"],[4728," updates"],[4728,".</"],[4728,"p"],[4728,">\n"],[4728," "],[4728," </"],[4728,"header"],[4734,">\n\n"],[4734," "],[4753," <"],[4766,"section"],[4768," class"],[4772,"=\""],[4783,"card"],[4794," stack"],[4